Marvel Studios and the Russo brothers  have given us several sneak peeks at  Avengers and game but comments from the  directors and tricks they've played on  the audience before have us wondering  whether what we've really seen tells us  the truth about what to expect from the  movie Trust is built over time and Joe  and Anthony Russo have proven that the  only thing we can really count on from  them is a well-made movie everything  else is questionable look no further  than the trailer for Avengers infinity  war one shot shows the entire team  including the Hulk running at the screen  in Wakanda but when the film arrived the  shot was nowhere to be found in an  interview with slash film Joe and  Anthony Russo admitted to changing  trailers to misdirect viewers saying at  our disposal are lots of different shots  that aren't in the movie that we can  manipulate through CG to tell a story  that we want to tell specifically for  the purpose of the trailer and not for  the film as many observers pointed out  Joe Russo also appeared to straight-up  lie about the title of Avengers endgame  when asked if it was ever spoken in  infinity war the director said no but  we're in the endgame when the first  trailer for endgame dropped reports  swirled that the movie's promotional  clips would only feature footage from  the first 15 or 20 minutes with a final  cut that clocks in at over three hours  that leaves a lot of the movie on scene  according to Marvel boss Kevin Feige  those reports are quote somewhat  accurate but the vagueness of his  comment leaves open the possibility that  Marvel could throw in a quick shot or  two from a later sequence it's hard to  believe that everything is coming from  the beginning of the movie there have  been plenty of clips of the team sulking  around in the aftermath of Thanos is  decimation but there have also been  several action sequences and a variety  of costume changes  Black Widow having both short blonde and  long red hair seems to indicate that a  lot of ground is being covered since  Iron Man and Captain America threw down  in Captain America's Civil War fans have  been anxiously awaiting the inevitable  reunion of Tony Stark and Steve Rogers  it seemed a safe bet that we'd get some  kind of movement between the two an  infinity war but it didn't happen the  end game special looks spot did reveal  an emotional scene  when the two heroes as they  reestablished their trust you trust me  and two fans everywhere rejoiced until  the Russos dropped a bomb in an  interview not long after Joe Russo  announced that the shot wasn't in the  movie  Anthony teased the different possibility  maybe it's in the movie the brothers  laughed with glee as they tortured  bewildered Marvel fans with the  possibility that we may not see Rodgers  and stark reconcile it's hard to believe  they deny the audience a chance to see  some closure for one of the cornerstone  relationships in the MCU but if it  happens it might look a lot different  than that one particular shocked  Hulk being inserted into infinity war  footage where he didn't belong let fans  know that all bets were off heading into  endgame promotion as the advance looks  have trickled out of Marvel's tightly  sealed vault the speculation has swung  from who's being added in to who's being  cropped out the Super Bowl spot in  particular got a ton of attention due to  a couple of shots that seemed to  deliberately leave gaps between  characters fans pointed out that a shot  showing cap and the team looking up into  the sky had a huge empty area while the  first shot of the crew's striding in  slo-mo threw the Avengers HQ hanger  seemed to also have an unevenly spaced  gap while speculation on this level  would normally be left for the most  obsessive fans the fact that we've seen  two completely different shots of Thor's  axe in the endgame trailers has made it  a topic of wider interest fans love  seeing the Green Machine do his thing  and yet we haven't seen him in action  since he's squared off against Thanos  and was soundly beaten during the  opening moments of infinity war the fact  that he's about to finish a three movie  story arc has fans on the edge of their  seats to see how his story will play out  many are expecting to finally see  Professor Hulk in action while others  think endgame may be the Jay giant swan  song whatever the case the fact that the  marketers refused to put a clip of Hulk  into the end game promotional footage is  maddening Bruce Banner has shown up  multiple times but the fact that the  Russos haven't allowed the slightest  glimpse of Green on the screen makes one  wonder what exactly they're hiding the  special look trailer finally had a shot  of Thanos geared up and ready for action  again he's covered head-to-toe  armored while apparently beaming down to  a location so why is he wearing armor as  infinity war plays out Thanos slowly  leaves his armor behind eventually  unneeded now that he has the Infinity  stones to protect him  perhaps the Infinity Gauntlet simply  broke during the snap which is a  scenario that Joe Russo has implied as  being plausible another possibility is  that the scene occurs while the Avengers  are traveling through time time travel  in the quantum realm are heavily  rumoured to play a big part in the movie  so there's a possibility that our heroes  could be fighting vanos in the past and  don't get sucked into a time vortex we  won't be able to save you it's fun to  get worked up over feeling betrayed by  the Russos but the truth is they're  doing it mostly out of love speaking  with Empire Joe Russo summed up the  directors feelings perfectly when he  said the thing that's most important to  us is that we preserve the surprise of  the narrative this talented pair of  directors isn't just trolling fans for  the fun of it they're aware that they're  sitting on a goldmine of information  that tens of millions of fans can't wait  to see they want the experience to be a  good one not spoiled by bad timing or  too much information Joe Russo added  when I was a kid and saw the Empire  Strikes Back at 11:00 a.m. on the day it  opened it so profoundly moved me because  I didn't know a damn thing about the  story I was going to watch we're trying  to replicate that experience check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about Avengers  endgame are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

